prompt:
Here's the motion for the menu drawer on our library site (Fernhill Library). A reviewer said it 'feels a bit off' but couldn't say why, so can you polish it?

<nav class="drawer" id="drawer" aria-hidden="true">...links...</nav>
<div class="scrim" id="scrim"></div>

.drawer {
  position: fixed; inset: 0 auto 0 0; width: 280px;
  transform: translateX(-100%);
  transition: transform 180ms cubic-bezier(0.5, 0, 0.9, 0.6);
  visibility: hidden;
}
.drawer.open {
  transform: translateX(0);
  transition: transform 240ms cubic-bezier(0.3, 0.7, 0.2, 1);
  visibility: visible;
}
.scrim { position: fixed; inset: 0; background: rgb(0 0 0 / 0.4); opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; transition: opacity 200ms linear; }
.scrim.open { opacity: 1; pointer-events: auto; }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .drawer { transform: none; opacity: 0; transition: opacity 120ms linear; }
  .drawer.open { opacity: 1; }
  .scrim { transition-duration: 120ms; }
}
